  "result": "`ArrayBuffer.prototype.maxByteLength` is implemented in its file only. All 20 runs under `built-ins/ArrayBuffer/prototype/maxByteLength/` pass, and clippy is clean.\n\nStep 3 is a comment, not a check. `kahvi-core` has no shared data block representation: `ArrayBufferData` has no shared flag, no `ObjectKind` creates a shared buffer, and the SharedArrayBuffer constructor is a not-implemented stub. The comment in the file points to that. I did not add a runtime check, since there is nothing to test against.\n\nFor steps 5\u20136 I replaced the `_ =>` fallback with a match on `max_byte_length`: `Some` reports the max, `None` reports the current byte length. The `TypeError` for the invariant is gone. I kept the inline slot check in step 2 because there is no `RequireInternalSlot` helper in `kahvi_core::ops`. The helpers come from `kahvi_core::object::typed_array`, since no `ops` equivalent exists.\n\nBLOCKED: no shared data block representation in kahvi-core, so IsSharedArrayBuffer (step 3) cannot be checked at runtime; the step is documented, not enforced.",
